From d3efa2260d5b57aa44567619902e02439bc05585 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:30:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_te_fill_in_role, v2_backup_te_activity,
 v2_backup_te_bands_silent, v2_backup_te_bands_pieces, v2_rb_participation_060

Backup-TE and silent-games RB layers, all candidates that missed their bars (2026-10-22 / 2026-10-25):
- v2_te_fill_in_role and v2_backup_te_activity (with the transfer of the freed volume to the TE1): the fill-in hypothesis was
  confirmed in the data but the factors fixed the level, not the error; the transfer to the TE1 was the part that hurt the start
  pool (the discount alone shipped as v2_backup_te_discount, EVERY-TE -0.023).
- v2_backup_te_bands_silent / _pieces and v2_rb_participation_060 (silent-layers run): none passed, each made EVERY-TE / EVERY-RB worse.
Kept: the shipped v2_backup_te_discount with BACKUP_TE_ACTIVITY_BANDS, backup_te_activity_multiplier, te_room_rank and
_te_last_snap_shares. Removes the fill-in role helpers, transfer_te_backup_volume, the silent band tables and backup_te_bands, the
RB 0.6 strength constant, and the tests of the removed flags. Default boards identical (.sweeps/board_identity.py, six in-season
scenarios 2023-2026, boards and explanations). Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
